  "notes": "USAGE:\nNot to be confused with the homophone {確率|かくりつ} (probability). {確立|かくりつ} means to establish firmly, while {確率|かくりつ} refers to mathematical probability. The kanji {立|りつ} (stand, establish) versus {率|りつ} (rate, ratio) distinguishes them in writing.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {制度|せいど}を{確立|かくりつ}する: to establish a system\n- {地位|ちい}を{確立|かくりつ}する: to establish one's position\n- {技術|ぎじゅつ}を{確立|かくりつ}する: to establish a technique\n- {方法|ほうほう}が{確立|かくりつ}される: a method is established\n- アイデンティティの{確立|かくりつ}: establishment of identity",
